            <div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-body field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><h3><strong>Vintage Village of Lights</strong>&nbsp;</h3>
<p class="paragraph"><span><strong>Fridays, Saturdays, and Sundays</strong> from 4 pm to 9 pm (final entry by 8 pm)<br>
<strong>November 28 through December 21, 2025&nbsp;</strong><br>
Cost: $26.14 per group, taxes included (up to six people per group; children under two are not counted toward the maximum group size).</span><br>
<strong><a href="https://anc.ca.apm.activecommunities.com/ottawa/activity/search?onlineSiteId=0&amp;locale=en-US&amp;activity_select_param=2&amp;activity_keyword=Vintage%20Village%20of%20Lights&amp;viewMode=list">Advance registration</a>.&nbsp;<span>Reminder! Only one registration ($26.14 taxes included) is required if your group includes six (6) or fewer people. </span></strong></p>
<p>Make memories to treasure at the Vintage Village of Lights. Enjoy a postcard-perfect 1920s and 30s heritage village charmingly decorated for the holidays. Explore festive vignettes and light displays, visit with Santa, decorate gingerbread cookies, complete a craft, take in a seasonal heritage skill demonstration, relax around the bonfire, and more. Fun for family and friends of all ages. Bonus! Browse a unique selection of handmade items and pick up the perfect gift in our Boutique. Drop by the canteen for cozy snacks and refreshments—including a selection of baked goods made with produce grown right here at the museum (while supplies last).</p>
<p>*The offered seasonal heritage skill demonstration may vary evening-to-evening depending on conditions and the availability of our skilled heritage interpreters.&nbsp;</p>
<p class="paragraph"><strong>Please review the notes below to help plan your visit.</strong></p>
<h4><span>Notes</span></h4>
<ul>
<li>Each registration&nbsp;<span>($26.14 taxes included)</span> includes entry to the Vintage Village of Lights for up to six visitors.<span>&nbsp;</span>If the address associated with your <a href="https://anc.ca.apm.activecommunities.com/ottawa/faq?locale=en-US">Register Ottawa</a> account is located outside Ottawa, a 25% non-resident fee applies.</li>
<li>Children under two years of age are not counted toward the 6 person per group maximum.&nbsp;</li>
<li>This event includes both indoor and outdoor activities. Please dress appropriately for weather conditions, including wind chill.&nbsp;</li>
<li>There is no public transit to the museum. Free parking is available on site.</li>
<li><strong>The event runs as scheduled in most weather conditions.</strong> <strong>Your registration will be honoured for the date and entry timeslot you selected at the time of booking.</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Your registration is non-refundable and non-transferable. </strong></li>
<li>The main pathways at the museum are packed gravel. Most buildings used for activities and demonstrations have ramp access, however, ramp access may not be available at every entry/exit point. Staff are happy to direct you to the nearest accessible entry or exit. Please note that because our heritage buildings were built to the standards of their time, a limited number of spaces may not be accessible to all.</li>
<li><a href="https://ottawa.ca/en/node/1007409/">Information about accessibility </a>can be found on the museum’s webpage.&nbsp;If you have questions regarding accessibility, please contact 613-580-2988 or <a href="mailto:museecumberlandmuseum@ottawa.ca">museecumberlandmuseum@ottawa.ca</a>.</li>
<li>In the rare event an evening is cancelled due to extreme weather or other unforeseen circumstances, updates will be published to the <a href="https://www.facebook.com/cumberlandmuseum">Cumberland Heritage Village Museum Facebook</a> page and all registered visitors will be contacted by email with further information.</li>
</ul>
